            "modules": [
              {
                "id": "context",
                "kind": "prose",
                "text": "The interesting part is where those things meet: when a powerful capability remains unfamiliar, its implications are unclear and a service must explain itself without overshadowing the experience."
              },
              {
                "id": "education",
                "kind": "prose",
                "text": "I studied Communication Design because I wanted to understand how ideas become clear through words, aesthetics, hierarchy, motion, systems and the interplay between them. Language taught me that meaning shifts with what is said and how it is carried.",
                "emphasis": [
                  {
                    "text": "Communication Design",
                    "tone": "blue"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "practice",
                "kind": "prose",
                "text": "Agency work sharpened my visual judgement, craft and pace. Product work showed me that behaviour, brand and trust often belong to the same problem.",
                "emphasis": [
                  {
                    "text": "Product work",
                    "tone": "blue"
                  }
                ]
              },
